{"address": "1201 Anacapa St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": false, "classy": true, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": true, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 4.0, "categories": "Donuts, Wine Bars, Bars, Breakfast & Brunch, Bakeries, American (New), Nightlife, Food, Coffee & Tea, Restaurants, Cafes", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": null, "name": "Cafe Ana", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2021-04-20 12:02:35", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "I've been wanting to check this place out for a little while now, and I finally had the chance to eat brunch here with a couple of friends (before the covid-19 closures). The food was delicious and I personally really loved their pastry basket. I can't wait until it's safe to eat in restaurants again because this is definitely going to be one of the first places I go to! Their pastry case looked amazing and they had so many menu items that intrigued me!"}, {"review_date": "2020-05-03 23:49:49", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "I hope this place opens soon. I just discovered it and really loved it."}, {"review_date": "2020-03-06 10:27:28", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "I love this cafe and so easy to run in for lunch while working in county building.  They are always clean and the food is great!  They are quick and friendly.  Their cheeseburger is the best cheeseburger I've had in a long time!
Grilled bun, super melty cheese and thick meat!  Good tomato and sauce is yum.  Love their chips and they make a Bloody Mary too.  There are days you need a bloody Mary to deal with the day.  Then walk back over to county bldg.  

Cafe always has nice staff.  I tip them well.  They make an amazing meal quick and what else can I ask for"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "330 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": true, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 3.5, "categories": "Mexican, Restaurants, Seafood", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "16:0-0:0", "Monday": "16:0-22:0", "Saturday": "10:0-0:0", "Sunday": "10:0-22:0", "Thursday": "16:0-22:0", "Tuesday": "16:0-22:0", "Wednesday": "16:0-22:0"}, "name": "Casa Blanca Restaurant", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2020-03-11 05:59:08", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "My friend and I came here for lunch on Saturday. I am not sure how it is at dinner, but for lunch there was no line so it was fast to get a table. The waiter was very thorough and accommodating. Both my friend and I had the blood orange margarita, which was so good because it had a jalapeño kick! But, don't worry it's not too spicy for anyone that is sensitive to spice, it was just right. 

We both ended up going with the combination plate; me the taco and enchilada and her the taco and tamale. To be honest the only reason why I didn't go with the mahi mahi taco was because it was singular (taco) versus the other tacos were plural in the name (tacos) and so I was expecting to get at least two tacos in the combo. However, only one came so I would ask that the menu be more clear. But, the food was delicious and we even had enough for leftovers. Both plates came with rice and beans too. 

There is an axxess deal for BOGO entree for lunch or dinner as well. So with all the food and drinks we had my friend and I were able to split it evenly for about $24 per person, which I think is a great deal for such a quality food."}, {"review_date": "2020-03-08 15:09:08", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Delicious food and drinks! Really fast service. Nice location with a nice scenic patio. They have heaters so you don't have to worry about getting cold. I ordered the burrito and my husband got the fajitas, both were delicious! I also got the margarita flight, which I highly recommend. If you're close to Amtrak on state, I would recommend stopping by!"}, {"review_date": "2020-03-01 05:02:35", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Ate at the bar tonight for my friends birthday. The bartender Dan, (tall, light and handsome) was attentive and took great care of us! Fast drinks with a warm welcoming personality, a great guy. Good food too! my Bf and I had the tacos.. simple but tasty! Thank you!"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "5 E Figueroa St", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": true, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": false, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 5.0, "categories": "Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Wineries, Arts & Entertainment, Wine Tasting Room, Wine Bars, Nightlife, Food", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "12:0-20:0", "Monday": "0:0-0:0", "Saturday": "12:0-20:0", "Sunday": "12:0-16:0", "Thursday": "12:0-19:0", "Wednesday": "12:0-19:0"}, "name": "August Ridge Vineyards", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2019-08-10 02:22:21", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "My wife and I eloped last fall and stopped in for an impromptu wine tasting during that weekend. It was the best tasting experience we have ever had! The service was unparalleled and the wine was absolutely delicious. (The gentleman that helped us was wearing a super cool hummingbird shirt.... Thanks for the tasting!)

I would highly recommend that if you ever find yourself in SB, you make it a point to stop by! I know we will when we make it back! Thanks for giving us one of our favorite memories of the weekend!"}, {"review_date": "2019-07-18 00:10:26", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Wow, such a fan! Came here for special event that included a tasting. I really love the Italian varietals offered which is kind of rare for this area since most of the wineries produce Rhône varietals. The winemaker himself shared details about the production of the wine which made it really interactive. I really like whites but they are all really enjoyable. My favorite white was the Pinot Grigio. 

Even as a local of four years, I had never visited any of the businesses in Arcada Plaza. I found out that many businesses there have a deal where they waive the corkage fee if you bring in a bottle from August Ridge, super great info! I would highly recommend this tasting room to friends who want to try out different varietals!"}, {"review_date": "2019-06-13 02:50:49", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Looking forward to coming here soon"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "3315 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": true, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "French, Cafes, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch, Food, Sandwiches, Bakeries", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "6:30-16:0", "Monday": "0:0-0:0", "Saturday": "6:30-16:0", "Sunday": "6:30-15:0", "Thursday": "6:30-16:0", "Tuesday": "6:30-16:0", "Wednesday": "6:30-16:0"}, "name": "Renaud's Patisserie & Bistro", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-18 18:26:49", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Wow wow wow! Stopped here on our way home to OC from Los Olivos and had their croissant egg breakfast sandwich, fresh squeezed OJ and chocolate croissant. Literally BEST. IVE. EVER. HAD! So excited we found a place for breakfast on our way home!"}, {"review_date": "2022-01-14 20:02:25", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Delicious croissant breakfast sandwich! Friendly staff, cute ambiance, quick service."}, {"review_date": "2022-01-05 17:09:20", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "We have enjoyed Renaud's many times, for breakfast, lunch, special desserts or just a snack. But I was really blown away this year by their Galette Des Rois (King's Cake) to celebrate Epiphany (January 6). 

I've had the traditional Mardi Gras style cake many times, either homemade or store bought. However, Renaud's has really WOWED me with the french style King's Cake!! It's everything I love about french pastries, buttery, light, delicious almond filling! It is just fantastic and so fun. 

The cake comes with two adorable little figurines to hide in the cake and a gold crown! It's such a fun cake to share and delicious with coffee. I really enjoyed this seasonal item and I can't wait to order another next year."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "217 E Anacapa St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": null, "hipster": null, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": null, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": false, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "no"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Restaurants, Mexican", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "10:30-15:30", "Monday": "10:30-15:30", "Saturday": "10:30-15:30", "Thursday": "10:30-15:30", "Tuesday": "10:30-15:30", "Wednesday": "10:30-15:30"}, "name": "Mony's Mexican Food", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-17 22:50:16", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "All four of us had an amazing experience. Guacamole is the thicker rather than creamy. More so a pico de gallo con guacamole. 

Burrito had some great fresh rice and beans! 

Give a try of the mole and mango salsa. We went back for more!"}, {"review_date": "2022-01-08 21:08:38", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "The tacos tasted unbelievably good, there was so much flavor in them which was the highlight."}, {"review_date": "2021-12-21 04:00:13", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Best tacos and salsa bar in SB. Very reasonable too, friendly staff. Avocado salsa is so yummy."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "113 W De La Guerra St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Juice Bars & Smoothies, Restaurants, Food, Vegan, Cafes, Bakeries, Coffee & Tea, Gluten-Free, Vegetarian, Acai Bowls", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "9:0-15:0", "Monday": "0:0-0:0", "Saturday": "9:0-15:0", "Sunday": "10:0-14:0", "Thursday": "9:0-15:0", "Tuesday": "9:0-15:0", "Wednesday": "9:0-15:0"}, "name": "Green Table", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-19 05:49:19", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Cute cafe with delicious healthy options.  Decided to stop in on our drive from LA to Santa Cruz. We specifically yelped in advance for healthy breakfast and lunch options as it's easy to eat junk when you are doing a long drive.  We had avocado toast and a banana strawberry  smoothie. Both were great.  Looking forward to trying it out again."}, {"review_date": "2021-11-27 20:47:58", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "This is simply one of the best places in Santa Barbara. I am so grateful to have discovered it. Before commenting on the excellent food, even better are the amazing women who work here. Having traveled the world, I've never seen a group of people more joyful and more delighted to be at work - in ANY profession. Whatever's going on in your life, you can be sure that their warm radiant welcome will lift your spirits. Whether you are a daily regular, as I have become, or a newcomer, as I once was, their enthusiasm that you have entered their spectacular oasis to share in it and their food, is unparalleled. They all take immense pride and joy in what they do.

I've often read that food prepared with love infuses that love into what you are eating. I never believed that until eating here. The food is fantastic. There are my favorites, from their Mamma Maca smoothie to the delicious Pesto Panini. Their fresh juices are unparalleled, clean in their taste and flavor combinations. And then there's the daily flavor of banana bread.  The other day I was there when the chef brought out a whole raw apple pie specially ordered for someone's Thanksgiving. She was glowing with pride for her creation, and the care the other women took in boxing it up was a sight to see. It wasn't just a pie, but rather something made special for someone's holiday.

I am vegan so I especially appreciate their vegan offerings. Their menu is organic, gluten-free, and locally sourced. You can really feel and taste the difference between food created at a chain by exhausted workers with cheaply-sourced, chemically-laden products, and food created by people with an exuberance for what they are doing and care in picking the perfect fresh ingredients for it. This should be a model for the world over."}, {"review_date": "2021-11-14 16:40:39", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Wonderful team and fabulous food. Their smoothies are to die for. The matcha lattee wow!!! Always smiling and helpful. My kids favorite place in Santa Barbara. I wish they would open another in Goleta."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "3707 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.0, "categories": "Restaurants, Sandwiches, Chicken Shop, Chicken Wings, Fast Food, Caterers, Event Planning & Services", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "10:30-22:0", "Monday": "0:0-0:0", "Saturday": "6:30-16:0", "Thursday": "6:30-22:0", "Tuesday": "6:30-22:0", "Wednesday": "6:30-22:0"}, "name": "Chick-fil-A", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-04 06:14:23", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "A top tier chick fil a that only appears once in a lifetime. Love the food and service at this location specifically. I know there are many different chick fil a's but this one in particular nails customer service. When they mess up on an order (which they rarely do) they always make sure to make it right! That's customer service which is pretty hard to find in the fast food industry."}, {"review_date": "2021-12-22 05:05:38", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Love it! Food is awesome every single time but not a big fan of the outdoor cleanliness"}, {"review_date": "2021-12-14 13:39:47", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Delicious as always!
Go to for fast food and the fries never disappoints.

Must try the peppermint milkshake at least once. I don't really even like milkshakes because I prefer to eat and not drink my ice cream, but this one was pretty yummy and I had multiple sips of my partners drink!"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "1049 Casitas Pass Rd", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": null, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Breakfast & Brunch, American (Traditional)", "city": "Carpinteria", "hours": {"Friday": "7:0-14:0", "Saturday": "7:0-14:0", "Sunday": "7:0-14:0", "Thursday": "7:0-14:0", "Tuesday": "7:0-14:0", "Wednesday": "7:0-14:0"}, "name": "Hugos Restaurant", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2021-12-15 18:08:24", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "We almost gave this place a pass - not a lot of upfront charm. But the Yelp reviews were good so we gave it a try. Glad we did! Friendly service as soon as we walked in. Basic breakfast was hot and delicious. I had scrambled eggs (fresh and yummy) with crispy hash browns and sourdough toast. My husband had the veggie scramble (zucchini, red peppers, onion, mushrooms) all fresh and delicious, with the same sides I had. Good cup of coffee, also! We appreciate a hard-working local restaurant and will definitely come back. Four stars just because the ambiance isn't really there. Don't let that stop you from giving this place a try!"}, {"review_date": "2021-11-27 01:28:40", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "We were coming home from a college visit trip to SLO and UCSB and wanted to hit Carp for breakfast. My kid typed in breakfast and this was one of the first that popped up - thank you Yelp!! Mom and pop-type small strip-mall cafe and we loved it. My wife and kids had pancakes (wife added blueberries) with eggs and I had the French toast. A side of hash browns to share (although we probably didn't need it) - just what the road trip ordered. Super friendly and when the people in front of us didn't need menus because the locals know what they want, it is a good sign. Hard working family, but open from 7am-2pm so it might not be a bad gig.... We will stop there again I am sure."}, {"review_date": "2021-10-09 16:17:22", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Hugo's Restaurant in Carpinteria is THE best breakfast/brunch spot. I especially love their pancakes, stir fried noodles, and chilaquiles! Their menu is so diverse and anyone can find something to their liking. 

The owners are so welcoming and joyful every time I visit. They have been operating for 20+ years! The service is phenomenal; you never have to wait long for your food. 

If you're ever in the area, this is the spot."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "938 Embarcadero Del Nrte", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.0, "categories": "Sandwiches, Restaurants, Burgers", "city": "Goleta", "hours": null, "name": "Javan's", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2014-02-25 06:54:05", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Sigh ... Javan's is no more :'(  I miss it already."}, {"review_date": "2013-09-10 00:43:52", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "It perplexes me that this place is always so empty. Honestly it is the best food in IV without a doubt and it's because the owners double as the cooks and are invested in the overall quality of their ingredients and product. They are always entertaining and you could learn a thing or two from just conversing with them during your lunch. Consider helping out this humble mom and pop shop before heading to a big franchise restaurant because they do not compromise anything in their menu and are competitively priced compared to the rest of IV. 

I would recommend the Tuna sandwich for it's delicious combination of dressings and tastiness of the fish. Every bite is savory and leaves you wanting more. You can't go wrong with any of the sandwiches really though."}, {"review_date": "2013-09-09 04:07:36", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "The owners of this place should seriously consider investing in a good quality sign for out front.  Currently they have an unlit vinyl sign so the place is basically unnoticeable, especially at night.  I bet they would really see business improve if they weren't cheap about the sign.

Good sandwiches and chili though."}], "state": "CA"}
